nd if it is stuck tap carefully sideways with\n     a soft hammer, do not lever off. • Ensure body is clean and align bolt holes in bearing housing/\n                              adaptor with body threads.\n    • Once body loose, remove bolts and washers completely while\n     supporting body.        • Fit all bolts with washers finger tight to hold body in place.\n                             • Tighten all bolts to torque shown in table.\n    5.07 Bearing Housing                               \n                             • Ensure body and adaptor/bearing housing sit flush.\n    Lip Seals                                          \n                             6.04 Seals                \n    • Both front and rear lip seals can be pulled out using either seal\n     pullers or with suitable pliers Single mechanical seals:\n    • Check lip seals for damage and replace as required. Static Face\n    Bearing removal          • Ensure seal is clean and free from damage.\n                             • Lubricate seal rubber and press seal into body bore.\n    • Bearing extractor or Arbor press may be required.\n                             • Ensure seal is fully home and square to shaft.\n    • Remove lips seal as above.                       \n    • Remove retaining rings use correct retaining ring pliers. Dynamic Face\n    • Press on the impeller end of the shaft to remove the shaft and • Ensure seal is clean and free from damage.\n     bearing assembly.                                 \n                           6                           ",
